; Wheel nodes sit exactly on the model's axles (reference_truck.gd hangs the
; authored tire, rim and bolts on them with no offset), so each tire spins
; around its own hub. The drawn tire is 0.544 m; the physics radius is larger
; by how far VehicleBody3D sinks each loaded axle below its ray contact
; (front 0.051, rear 0.026, measured), so the rubber sits exactly on the road.
; Mount heights put both axles at the model's wheel centre (y -0.122) once
; settled, with the body level at 0.666 m above the ground.
